{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The `search` service had no pods, and I fixed that and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned status 200.\n\nThe namespace has a `memory-limit-quota` that requires every container to specify a memory limit. The `search` deployment had none, so its ReplicaSet couldn't create a pod. With no pod behind the `search` service, requests that depend on it failed.\n\nI ran `kubectl set resources deploy search -n hotel-reservation --limits=memory=256Mi --requests=memory=128Mi`. The `search` pod is now Running, and the `search` service has endpoints again.\n\nI didn't run any end-user requests against the application myself, so the only checks were the pod and endpoint state. I didn't check the other deployments for the same missing memory limit. They were already running, so the quota didn't block them."}}
